A||||9||batboy||The V8 Batmobile Fiero lives!||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||04-15-2001||04:00 PM||||It's alive! I've brought the beast back to life. Got the license plate tags and insurance caught back up, ($$$) so I tinkered around on it this weekend in between other projects. Of my 3 extra batteries, only one would hold a charge. Changed a leaking valve cover gasket on the ol' 350 and fixed the exhaust manifold donut leak. Did a few other repairs that I had been putting off, then cleaned it up a little (interior was a mess).<P>Considering I haven't drove it since maybe last November and that motor is dang near wore out, it fired up fairly easily. Ran a little rough and grumbled for a while until it warmed up good. Looks like it's still burning a little oil (smoking a bit under load), but at least all of the leaks are under control now.<P>Just got back from a little Easter Sunday cruise, since the weather if fine today. Had the Sunroof open, windows down, and the stereo blasting. <B>SWEET!</B> Almost forgot how much fun my little Batmobile was to drive. Nothing like a V8 noisily rumbling a few inches from your backside.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batkid3.gif">    <B>BATBOY</B><BR>1985 SE auto with 350 Chevy V8 (Batmobile),<BR>suspension mods, lowered, GA brakes, battery<BR>relocated up front, stereo mods, etc...||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||04-15-2001||04:01 PM||||<P>got pics!?||||reg||5
Z||000002||Formula88||04-15-2001||04:22 PM||||V8 Fiero.<BR>Got Cubes?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It's a great feeling, huh?  I just got my beast running after it was broken down for 2 weeks, and that was after only having her running for a week after putting a new clutch in (down for a few more weeks waiting on parts).  Yea, it's a great feeling and summer is almost here!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||04-15-2001||04:51 PM||||When ya gonna get that built 350 in there?  It'll be a freakin' monster when ya get that beast in there!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||04-15-2001||05:34 PM||||It's a real shame, huh. I've had a 1988 Z-28 roller 350 short block built for well over a year now. TRW forged flattop pistons, bored 0.030", decked, reconditioned truck rods, crank turned and straightened, balanced, Comp Cams 270 roller cam and roller lifters, true roller timing set, etc... Just need to find a good pair of high performance aluminum heads to finish it off the top end. First it was not enough money, now it's not enough time. Hopefully, one of these days...<P>Oh, so you wanna see pics. The old timers used to get tired of me posting pics all the time of my raggity ol' Batmobile (haha). Check out my website if you really MUST to see more.<P> <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/batmobile" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/batmobile</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/batmobile-collage.jpg"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||1
